        {"name": "micron::conjunction", "header": "type_traits.hpp", "covers": ["micron::disjunction", "micron::negation"], "summary": "Combines Boolean trait types, selecting the first false operand or the final operand when all are true.", "sections": [{"title": "Related templates", "paragraphs": ["`conjunction<>` is true; `disjunction<>` is false. `disjunction<Bs...>` selects the first true operand or the final operand when all are false. `negation<B>` negates `bool(B::value)`. `_v` forms expose the Boolean result. The class templates select through the pack rather than evaluating every later operand's `value` unconditionally."]}]},
        {"name": "micron::rank", "header": "type_traits.hpp", "covers": ["micron::extent", "micron::alignment_of"], "summary": "Reports the number of built-in array dimensions. The size-property traits return unsigned compile-time values.", "sections": [{"title": "Related templates", "paragraphs": ["`rank<T>` and `rank_v<T>` count built-in array dimensions. `extent<T,I>` and `extent_v<T,I>` report dimension `I`, or zero for a non-array, unknown bound, or absent dimension. `alignment_of<T>` and `alignment_of_v<T>` report `alignof(T)`; `T` must meet the completeness requirements."]}]},
        {"name": "micron::aligned_storage", "header": "type_traits.hpp", "covers": ["micron::aligned_storage_t", "micron::aligned_union", "micron::aligned_union_t"], "summary": "Supplies an aligned byte-storage type without constructing an object in it.", "sections": [{"title": "Storage templates", "paragraphs": ["`aligned_storage<Len,Align>::type` contains `unsigned char[Len]` aligned to `Align`; the default alignment comes from the compiler's maximally aligned empty helper. `aligned_union<Len,Ts...>::type` uses the greatest alignment of `Ts...` and a length at least `Len` and the largest `sizeof(Ts)`. The union form requires at least one type and exposes `alignment_value`. `_t` aliases select the storage types. Object lifetime and destruction remain the caller's responsibility."]}]},
        {"name": "micron::invoke_result", "header": "type_traits.hpp", "covers": ["micron::invoke_result_t", "micron::result_of", "micron::result_of_t", "micron::is_invocable", "micron::is_invocable_r", "micron::is_nothrow_invocable", "micron::is_nothrow_invocable_r"], "summary": "Names the result of invoking `Fn` with `Args...` through a nested `type`, when that invocation is valid.", "sections": [{"title": "Callable traits", "paragraphs": ["Invocation handling distinguishes ordinary callables, pointers to member functions, and pointers to data members, with direct and dereferenced object forms. `invoke_result_t` selects `type`. The deprecated `result_of<Fn(Args...)>` and `result_of_t` expose the older signature form.", "`is_invocable` tests availability; `is_invocable_r<R,...>` additionally tests result conversion to `R`. The `is_nothrow_invocable` and `is_nothrow_invocable_r` forms include exception specifications and result conversion. A declaration of `reference_wrapper` supports trait unwrapping, but `type_traits.hpp` does not define that wrapper class. `declval<T>()` supplies a type expression for unevaluated operands and is deliberately ill-formed if evaluated."]}]},
        {"name": "micron::index_sequence", "header": "type_traits.hpp", "covers": ["micron::make_index_sequence", "micron::index_sequence_for", "micron::concat_index_sequence", "micron::make_index_sequence_impl"], "summary": "Represents a compile-time pack of unsigned indices. `size()` returns the number of indices.", "sections": [{"title": "Sequence construction", "paragraphs": ["`make_index_sequence<N>` produces indices 0 through `N-1`; `index_sequence_for<Ts...>` uses `sizeof...(Ts)` as the count. The implementation recursively splits the count into halves. `concat_index_sequence<A,B>::type` appends the indices in `B` after adding the length of `A` to each of them; it is an offset concatenation. `make_index_sequence_impl<N>` is the named construction helper; its nested `type` is the public alias result."]}]},
        {"name": "micron::arg_type", "header": "type_traits.hpp", "covers": ["micron::arg_type_t"], "summary": "Extracts the single parameter type of a supported unary function signature.", "sections": [{"title": "Supported forms", "paragraphs": ["Specializations accept unary free functions, function pointers, and unary member functions with or without `const`. Pointer and reference wrappers are stripped recursively. `arg_type_t<F>` selects the nested `type`. The primary template has no definition; general callable classes, overloaded call operators, multiple parameters, and additional member qualifiers have no general extraction path."]}]},
